\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Full and empty observations}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{For the full selector #{P=I}, the [retained vacuum embedding](fdip-00HG) is the
ground-state change of density from #{L^2(\nu_0)} to #{L^2(dq)}. For #{P=0}, the
retained functions are scalars and their image is the vacuum line #{\mathbb C\psi_0}.
The compressed operators in both cases form semigroups, as verified in
\ref{fdip-00HI}.}

\p{A proper nonzero selector retains fewer position observables while the full
Hamiltonian still couples all coordinates. The [coupled chain](fdip-00GV) supplies
this situation already at two sites. Its vacuum marginal comes from #{\psi_0^2dq}; a
density proportional to #{\ue^{-U}} or a single discrete transfer weight uses different
state data.}
